1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,234
01 / SSH PROFILE: Add a deployment host with its address, SSH port, username, and authentication.

2
00:00:10,234 --> 00:00:11,359
02 / CONNECT: Save & connect opens the terminal. Credentials are not sent until the server key is trusted.

3
00:00:11,359 --> 00:00:17,812
VERIFY FINGERPRINT: Compare the Ed25519 SHA-256 fingerprint through a trusted channel before accepting.

4
00:00:17,812 --> 00:00:22,843
SSH TERMINAL: Connected as deploy on staging-web. Confirm the hostname and current load.

5
00:00:22,843 --> 00:00:27,281
03 / AI ASSISTANT: Open AI Assistant. The demo provider is already configured and tool-calling verified.

6
00:00:27,281 --> 00:00:36,359
SELECT TARGET: Use @ to target staging-web explicitly; the selected host scopes this request.

7
00:00:36,359 --> 00:00:41,968
RUN DIAGNOSTICS: The assistant checks disk space and service state before proposing a privileged change.

8
00:00:41,968 --> 00:00:47,828
04 / REVIEW COMMAND: Review the host and exact command: sudo systemctl restart nginx. Approve only this command.

9
00:00:47,828 --> 00:00:54,531
VERIFY RESULT: After approval, Selai runs the command and the assistant verifies nginx again.

10
00:00:54,531 --> 00:00:58,781
COMPLETE: nginx is active; restart exit code is 0. The response includes disk usage and the target host.
